ode loop, so one decode choke point per bridge suffices\"\n26|    },\n27|    {\n28|      \"id\": \"EVD-003\",\n29|      \"kind\": \"code\",\n30|      \"ref\": \"bridges/opencode-zen-bridge/server.py:ToolCallParser._drain/_flush_all/_classify_open\",\n31|      \"claim\": \"A rejected closed block is emitted to on_content as ONE piece open_tag+inner+close_tag, an unclosed tail as one piece starting at the open tag, a quoted tag as the bare tag; parsed blocks are never emitted as content, so a piece-level sink filter is sound\"\n32|    },\n33|    {\n34|      \"id\": \"EVD-004\",\n35|      \"kind\": \"command\",\n36|      \"ref\": \"shasum -a 256 bridges/opencode-zen-bridge/server.py ~/.dsh/bridges/opencode-zen-bridge/server.py; grep -n 'holding\\\\[0\\\\]\\\\|_PrefixDedup\\\\|MAX_TOTAL_SPAWNS' on both files\",\n37|      \"claim\": \"Repo copy (untracked) = stale snapshot sha d619476e/3148 lines; live = sha 5f6b7cb0/3885 lines with _PrefixDedup instead of held/holding, MAX_TOTAL_SPAWNS and _RequestAttempts; a copy of live runs 360 tests with 3 pre-existing failures; repo copy lacks tests/dsh_tools_fixture.json and tests/fixtures\"\n38|    },\n39|    {\n40|      \"id\": \"EVD-005\",\n41|      \"kind\": \"command\",\n42|      \"ref\": \"isolated scratch copy inside the run dir (removed afterwards): prototype of _recover_trailing_braces, function unwrap, _find_close_in, _strip_broken_tool_blocks + probes + unittest of 6 existing modules\",\n43|      \"claim\": \"Production payload with }, }}, '} }\\\\n}' tails and raw-newline variant parse to a bash call; '{broken', unterminated and under-closed stay None; OpenAI function envelope parses; name wins over function; 209 existing tests (lenient 5, emulation 28, step_interruption 95, native_fallback 14, stream_thinking 15, google_direct 52) OK; root tests.test_tool_parser 44 OK; 60 KiB parse 0.23 ms, strip 1.97 ms\"\n44|    },\n45|    {\n46|      \"id\": \"EVD-006\",\n47|      \"kind\": \"document\",\n48|      \"ref\": \"analysis/opencode-zen-tool-invoke-fix/evidence-ledger.md [F-01],[F-02],[F-07],[F-11]; tests/test_tool_parser.py:TestCrossBridgeParserContract\",\n49|      \"claim\": \"Production incident (bash heredoc with }}} in re-prompt 1/2 leaked and polluted re-prompt 2/2), negative-control tests that must stay green, id-rendering test, and the cross-bridge parity contract\"\n50|    }\n51|  ],\n52|  \"risk_triggers\": [],\n53|  \"assumptions\": [\n54|    {\n55|      \"id\": \"ASM-001\",\n56|      \"statement\": \"A complete top-level JSON object followed only by whitespace and extra '}' is an over-closed envelope of the same call, never different intended structure; other tails (commas, keys, text) stay rejected\",\n57|      \"status\": \"VALIDATED\",\n58|      \"class\": \"continuable\",\n59|      \"evidence_ids\": [\n60|        \"EVD-001\",\n61|        \"EVD-005\",\n62|        \"EVD-006\"\n63|      ]\n64|    },\n65|    {\n66|      \"id\": \"ASM-002\",\n67|      \"statement\": \"The repo copy of opencode-zen-bridge is a stale untracked snapshot of the live bridge; the design is anchored on symbols and invariants, the Coder re-baselines on current live before editing, and deploys as a patch guarded by a sha check, never as an overwrite\",\n68|      \"status\": \"VALIDATED\",\n69|      \"class\": \"continuable\",\n70|      \"evidence_ids\": [\n71|        \"EVD-004\",\n72|        \"EVD-003\"\n73|      ]\n74|    }\n75|  ],\n76|  \"verification_surface\": [\n77|    {\n78|      \"id\": \"VER-001\",\n79|      \"requirement_ids\": [\n80|        \"REQ-001\",\n81|        \"REQ-003\",\n82|        \"REQ-004\",\n83|        \"AD-001\",\n84|        \"AD-003\",\n85|        \"AD-004\",\n86|        \"BND-002\",\n87|        \"CD-001\"\n88|      ],\n89|      \"kind\": \"command\",\n90|      \"command\": \"python3 -m unittest tests.test_tool_parser -v\",\n91|      \"expected\": \"exit 0; 44 existing + new cross-bridge cases (trailing }}} and }}}}\\\\n, OpenAI function wrapper, name wins, malformed stays text) pass for core/tool_emulation.py and muse-bridge\",\n92|      \"environment\": \"local-python3\",\n93|      \"owner\": \"verifier\"\n94|    },\n95|    {\n96|      \"id\": \"VER-002\",\n97|      \"requirement_ids\": [\n98|        \"REQ-001\",\n99|        \"REQ-002\",\n100|        \"REQ-003\",\n101|        \"REQ-004\",\n102|        \"AD-001\",\n103|        \"AD-002\",\n104|        \"AD-003\",\n105|        \"BND-001\",\n106|        \"QA-001\",\n107|        \"CD-001\"\n108|      ],\n109|      \"kind\": \"command\",\n110|      \"command\": \"cd bridges/opencode-zen-bridge && python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .\",\n111|      \"expected\": \"exit 0, or the failure set exactly equals receipts/baseline-failures.txt recorded at Coder step 0 on the re-baselined live copy (currently 3 test_unmapped_* tests); test count = baseline + new tests; 0 errors\",\n112|      \"environment\": \"local-python3\",\n113|      \"owner\": \"verifier\"\n114|    },\n115|    {\n116|      \"id\": \"VER-003\",\n117|      \"requirement_ids\": [\n118|        \"REQ-001\",\n119|        \"REQ-002\",\n120|        \"REQ-003\",\n121|        \"AD-002\",\n122|        \"AD-003\",\n123|        \"BND-001\",\n124|        \"RISK-001\",\n125|        \"RISK-002\"\n126|      ],\n127|      \"kind\": \"command\",\n128|      \"command\": \"cd bridges/opencode-zen-bridge && python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t . -k negative_control -k unparsed_block_returned_as_text -k closed_batch_without_intermediate_close_kept -k sanitize_closed_alt_batch_kept -k broken_block -k history_renders_tool_calls\",\n129|      \"expected\": \"exit 0, Ran >= 6: F-07 negative controls, kept-batch sanitizer tests, id rendering and the new broken_block stream/json/sanitize/prompt tests all pass\",\n130|      \"environment\": \"local-python3\",\n131|      \"owner\": \"verifier\"\n132|    },\n133|    {\n134|      \"id\": \"VER-004\",\n135|      \"requirement_ids\": [\n136|        \"QA-002\",\n137|        \"AD-001\",\n138|        \"AD-002\",\n139|        \"RISK-002\"\n140|      ],\n141|      \"kind\": \"command\",\n142|      \"command\": \"cd bridges/opencode-zen-bridge && python3 -c \\\"import json,sys,time; sys.path.insert(0,'.'); import server as s; ok=json.dumps(dict(name='bash',arguments=dict(command='x'*60000))); big=ok+'}}}'; bad=ok[:-4]; blk='<tool_invoke>'+bad+'</tool_invoke>'; f=lambda fn,a: (lambda t: ([fn(a) for _ in range(20)], (time.perf_counter()-t)/20*1000)[1])(time.perf_counter()); a=f(s._parse_tool_call_blocks,big); b=f(s._parse_tool_call_blocks,bad); c=f(s._strip_broken_tool_blocks,blk); print(round(a,3),round(b,3),round(c,3)); sys.exit(0 if s._parse_tool_call_blocks(big) and s._parse_tool_call_blocks(bad) is None and s._strip_broken_tool_blocks(blk)==('',1) and max(a,b,c)<5 else 1)\\\"\",\n143|      \"expected\": \"exit 0; per-call time < 5 ms for 60 KiB parse with }}}, 60 KiB unterminated parse (None) and 60 KiB broken-block strip (('',1)); prototype pre-flight 0.23/0.16/1.97 ms\",\n144|      \"environment\": \"local-python3\",\n145|      \"owner\": \"verifier\"\n146|    }\n147|  ],\n148|  \"decisions\": [\n149|    {\n150|      \"id\": \"AD-001\",\n151|      \"status\": \"APPROVED\",\n152|      \"kind\": \"two-way\",\n153|      \"question\": \"Where and how to tolerate extra closing braces after a complete tool-call JSON object?\",\n154|      \"choice\": \"After json.loads and json.loads(strict=False) fail, raw_decode the first value and accept it iff it is a dict and the tail is non-empty, contains '}' and consists only of whitespace and '}'; in _loads_lenient for opencode-zen and via a local _loads_tolerant helper in core/tool_emulation.py and muse-bridge; _parse_tool_call_blocks and _normalize_arguments unchanged\",\n155|      \"alternatives\": [\n156|        \"Regex-strip trailing '}' from the text before json.loads\",\n157|        \"Brace-balance repair of the raw text\",\n158|        \"Patch a raw_decode loop inside _parse_tool_call_blocks (loop does not exist in current code)\"\n159|      ],\n160|      \"drivers\": [\n161|        \"Single decode choke point per bridge\",\n162|        \"Cold path only, zero extra I/O\",\n163|        \"Negative controls ({broken, under-closed) must still return None\"\n164|      ],\n165|      \"consequences\": [\n166|        \"Over-closed envelopes now execute; counted by log line tool_call_recovered\",\n167|        \"core and muse keep their strict control-character behaviour (baseline debt, not widened)\"\n168|      ],\n169|      \"approval_required\": false,\n170|      \"confirmation\": {\n171|        \"kind\": \"test\",\n172|        \"command\": \"python3 -m unittest tests.test_tool_parser -v\",\n173|        \"expected\": \"exit 0; trailing-brace cases recovered, broken payloads still rejected in core and muse\"\n174|      }\n175|    },\n176|    {\n177|      \"id\": \"AD-002\",\n178|      \"status\": \"APPROVED\",\n179|      \"kind\": \"two-way\",\n180|      \"question\": \"How to guarantee no raw <tool_call>/<tool_invoke> block reaches client content or the next incomplete-step re-prompt, independent of the held/dedup implementation?\",\n181|      \"choice\": \"Pure helper _strip_broken_tool_blocks(text)->(text,dropped) applied at three sinks: the ToolCallParser content sink in Handler._stream_sse (all attempts), Handler._serve_json right after _split_tool_calls, and _incomplete_tool_step_prompt; plus a one-line bridge notice when something was dropped and nothing else is visible; _is_incomplete_tool_step keeps reading raw attempt_texts so retry behaviour and caps are unchanged\",\n182|      \"alternatives\": [\n183|        \"Defer and strip the held buffer until the retry decision (handoff REQ-002 literal; absent in live code, reorders the retry chain)\",\n184|        \"Add an on_unparsed callback to ToolCallParser\",\n185|        \"Change _split_tool_calls to drop unparsed blocks (breaks F-07 tests)\"\n186|      ],\n187|      \"drivers\": [\n188|        \"Baseline-neutral: works on the stale snapshot and on live\",\n189|        \"Smallest diff and same invariant for SSE and JSON\",\n190|        \"Zero leaked raw tags error budget\"\n191|      ],\n192|      \"consequences\": [\n193|        \"An unquoted unparseable tool-tag example printed by the model is dropped (RISK-002)\",\n194|        \"Scan is capped at 16 candidate tags and fails open\"\n195|      ],\n196|      \"approval_required\": false,\n197|      \"confirmation\": {\n198|        \"kind\": \"test\",\n199|        \"command\": \"cd bridges/opencode-zen-bridge && python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t . -k broken_block\",\n200|        \"expected\": \"exit 0; no raw tag in SSE/JSON content or re-prompt, retries within caps, notice only when nothing else is visible\"\n201|      }\n202|    },\n203|    {\n204|      \"id\": \"AD-003\",\n205|      \"status\": \"APPROVED\",\n206|      \"kind\": \"two-way\",\n207|      \"question\": \"How to stop leaked or old broken closed blocks from poisoning replayed history and accept the OpenAI function envelope echoed inside a tool tag?\",\n208|      \"choice\": \"_sanitize_assistant_text additionally strips closed blocks whose inner is not parseable (valid closed single or batch blocks and quoted/fenced tags are kept byte-identical); _parse_tool_call_block in all three bridges unwraps obj['function'] only when top-level 'name' is absent; _render_tool_call unchanged\",\n209|      \"alternatives\": [\n210|        \"Strip every closed block regardless of validity\",\n211|        \"Reject the OpenAI function wrapper as malformed\"\n212|      ],\n213|      \"drivers\": [\n214|        \"test_closed_batch_without_intermediate_close_kept, test_sanitize_closed_alt_batch_kept and test_history_renders_tool_calls_and_results must stay green\",\n215|        \"Model echoes its own history format including id\"\n216|      ],\n217|      \"consequences\": [\n218|        \"Top-level name always wins; a present-but-invalid top-level name is still rejected\"\n219|      ],\n220|      \"approval_required\": false,\n221|      \"confirmation\": {\n222|        \"kind\": \"test\",\n223|        \"command\": \"cd bridges/opencode-zen-bridge && python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t . -k sanitize -k function_wrapper\",\n224|        \"expected\": \"exit 0; malformed closed block stripped, valid batches kept, wrapper parsed\"\n225|      }\n226|    },\n227|    {\n228|      \"id\": \"AD-004\",\n229|      \"status\": \"APPROVED\",\n230|      \"kind\": \"two-way\",\n231|      \"question\": \"How to keep three standalone parsers consistent and ship safely when the repo copy of opencode-zen-bridge is stale relative to live?\",\n232|      \"choice\": \"Keep three independent stdlib copies with parity enforced by extending TestCrossBridgeParserContract; Coder re-baselines the untracked bridge copy on current live first and deploys opencode-zen as a patch guarded by a sha256 comparison with the recorded baseline, backup in ~/work/backups, launchctl kickstart; core and muse ship via MR\",\n233|      \"alternatives\": [\n234|        \"Shared module imported by all bridges\",\n235|        \"Fix only opencode-zen-bridge\",\n236|        \"Overwrite live server.py with the repo copy\"\n237|      ],\n238|      \"drivers\": [\n239|        \"Each bridge deploys as a single standalone script\",\n240|        \"Live carries ~737 lines of newer spawn-budget work that an overwrite would revert\",\n241|        \"Cross-bridge contract test already exists\"\n242|      ],\n243|      \"consequences\": [\n244|        \"Three copies must be edited together\",\n245|        \"Rollout needs a merge step when live moved after re-baseline\"\n246|      ],\n247|      \"approval_required\": false,\n248|      \"confirmation\": {\n249|        \"kind\": \"test\",\n250|        \"command\": \"python3 -m unittest tests.test_tool_parser.TestCrossBridgeParserContract -v\",\n251|        \"expected\": \"exit 0; core/tool_emulation.py and muse-bridge give identical (calls, content) for all contract cases including the new ones\"\n252|      }\n253|    }\n254|  ],\n255|  \"quality_scenarios\": [\n256|    {\n257|      \"id\": \"QA-001\",\n258|      \"quality\": \"reliability\",\n259|      \"source\": \"GLM-5.3-Flash (Zen) Max via opencode-zen-bridge\",\n260|      \"stimulus\": \"emits <tool_invoke>{...bash heredoc...}}}</tool_invoke> (escaped or raw newlines) during incomplete_tool_step re-prompt 1/2, or emits a genuinely broken block\",\n261|      \"environment\": \"local bridge 127.0.0.1:9883, streaming and non-streaming, up to 8 concurrent turns\",\n262|      \"artifact\": \"_loads_lenient, _parse_tool_call_block(s), ToolCallParser sink in Handler._stream_sse, Handler._serve_json, _incomplete_tool_step_prompt\",\n263|      \"response\": \"over-closed block executes as a bash tool call on the first attempt; a broken block is neither streamed nor fed to the next re-prompt and retries stay within caps\",\n264|      \"response_measure\": \"1 tool call and 1 upstream spawn (was 3) for the production payload; 0 raw <tool_call>/<tool_invoke> in SSE/JSON content or re-prompt text; spawns <= NATIVE_RETRY_LIMIT+1\",\n265|      \"verification_ids\": [\n266|        \"VER-002\",\n267|        \"VER-003\"\n268|      ]\n269|    },\n270|    {\n271|      \"id\": \"QA-002\",\n272|      \"quality\": \"performance\",\n273|      \"source\": \"opencode-zen-bridge request thread\",\n274|      \"stimulus\": \"60 KiB tool-call block with trailing braces, 60 KiB unterminated block, 60 KiB broken block to strip\",\n275|      \"environment\": \"CPython 3 stdlib, single request thread, cold error path\",\n276|      \"artifact\": \"_recover_trailing_braces, _parse_tool_call_blocks, _strip_broken_tool_blocks\",\n277|      \"response\": \"linear decode/scan with a 16-candidate cap on the strip scan; no regex backtracking\",\n278|      \"response_measure\": \"< 5 ms per call at p95 (prototype 0.23 / 0.16 / 1.97 ms)\",\n279|      \"verification_ids\": [\n280|        \"VER-004\"\n281|      ]\n282|    }\n283|  ],\n284|  \"boundaries\": [\n285|    {\n286|      \"id\": \"BND-001\",\n287|      \"component\": \"bridges/opencode-zen-bridge/server.py parser and sanitizer layer\",\n288|      \"responsibility\": \"Decode tool-call blocks (with trailing-brace recovery and OpenAI envelope), strip unparseable raw blocks at content sinks, sanitize replayed history\",\n289|      \"allowed_dependencies\": [\n290|        \"json\",\n291|        \"re\",\n292|        \"existing module helpers (_code_context, _open_tag_at, _parse_tool_call_blocks, _RAW_CALL_RE, _log)\"\n293|      ],\n294|      \"forbidden_dependencies\": [\n295|        \"changing _split_tool_calls or ToolCallParser emit semantics\",\n296|        \"I/O or module-level mutable state inside helpers\",\n297|        \"changing _render_tool_call or retry caps\"\n298|      ],\n299|      \"verification_ids\": [\n300|        \"VER-002\",\n301|        \"VER-003\"\n302|      ]\n303|    },\n304|    {\n305|      \"id\": \"BND-002\",\n306|      \"component\": \"core/tool_emulation.py and bridges/muse-bridge/server.py _parse_tool_call_block\",\n307|      \"responsibility\": \"Accept trailing-brace tails and the OpenAI function envelope with unchanged strict decoding\",\n308|      \"allowed_dependencies\": [\n309|        \"json\",\n310|        \"local _recover_trailing_braces/_loads_tolerant helpers\"\n311|      ],\n312|      \"forbidden_dependencies\": [\n313|        \"cross-bridge or core imports from bridges\",\n314|        \"touching ToolCallParser or muse strict_live/LiveParserError semantics\",\n315|        \"adding lenient control-character decoding\"\n316|      ],\n317|      \"verification_ids\": [\n318|        \"VER-001\"\n319|      ]\n320|    }\n321|  ],\n322|  \"contract_deltas\": [\n323|    {\n324|      \"id\": \"CD-001\",\n325|      \"type\": \"behavior\",\n326|      \"producer\": \"opencode-zen-bridge, core/tool_emulation.py, muse-bridge tool-call parsers and opencode-zen Handler\",\n327|      \"consumer\": \"OpenAI-compatible clients (opencode, DSH) and the model re-prompt loop\",\n328|      \"change\": \"Previously rejected tool-call blocks with trailing '}' or an OpenAI function envelope now parse into tool calls; unparseable raw tool-tag blocks are no longer returned in assistant content or fed into re-prompts; a one-line bridge notice may be returned instead of an empty reply\",\n329|      \"compatibility\": \"Backward compatible: no schema, field, header or status-code change; only inputs that previously failed are accepted; clients never relied on raw rejected tags; state/*.json unchanged; explicitly required by REQ-002 of this task\",\n330|      \"verification_ids\": [\n331|        \"VER-001\",\n332|        \"VER-002\"\n333|      ]\n334|    }\n335|  ],\n336|  \"views\": [\n337|    {\n338|      \"id\": \"VIEW-001\",\n339|      \"type\": \"component\",\n340|      \"question\": \"Which parser/handler components change, which stay frozen, and how is cross-bridge parity enforced?\",\n341|      \"artifact_ref\": \"architecture/arch-spec.md\"\n342|    },\n343|    {\n344|      \"id\": \"VIEW-002\",\n345|      \"type\": \"dynamic\",\n346|      \"question\": \"How does the production }}} block and a genuinely broken block flow through parser, handler, SSE client and re-prompt after the fix?\",\n347|      \"artifact_ref\": \"architecture/arch-spec.md\"\n348|    }\n349|  ],\n350|  \"risks\": [\n351|    {\n352|      \"id\": \"RISK-001\",\n353|      \"scenario\": \"Trailing-brace recovery accepts an over-closed envelope that the model intended differently and executes a tool with unintended structure\",\n354|      \"probability\": \"low\",\n355|      \"impact\": \"medium\",\n356|      \"mitigation\": \"Accept only a dict followed by whitespace and '}' (tails with commas, keys or text are rejected), arguments must still be a dict, log line tool_call_recovered counts occurrences\",\n357|      \"verification_ids\": [\n358|        \"VER-001\",\n359|        \"VER-003\"\n360|      ]\n361|    },\n362|    {\n363|      \"id\": \"RISK-002\",\n364|      \"scenario\": \"Residual or over-strip: scan cap leaves tags in pathological text, an unquoted unparseable tag example is dropped, or first-attempt output changes\",\n365|      \"probability\": \"low\",\n366|      \"impact\": \"low\",\n367|      \"mitigation\": \"Quoted, fenced and valid blocks preserved; 16-candidate cap fails open with a log line; notice instead of an empty reply; history sanitizer as second line; targeted tests and perf gate\",\n368|      \"verification_ids\": [\n369|        \"VER-003\",\n370|        \"VER-004\"\n371|      ]\n372|    }\n373|  ],\n374|  \"threat_model\": {\n375|    \"required\": false,\n376|    \"assets\": [],\n377|    \"trust_boundaries\": [],\n378|    \"threats\": []\n379|  },\n380|  \"evolution\": {\n381|    \"compatibility\": \"Additive tolerance plus removal of rejected raw tags from content; OpenAI SSE/JSON schema, status codes and state/*.json unchanged; core and muse keep strict control-character decoding\",\n382|    \"migration\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE: no data, schema or state-file change; the only prerequisite is re-baselining the untracked repo copy of opencode-zen-bridge on current live (arch-spec section 9, step 0)\",\n383|    \"rollout\": \"Re-baseline on live, implement, VER-001..VER-004 green, compare live server.py sha256 with the recorded baseline (equal: copy; different: merge-file/patch the diff onto live and re-run VER), back up the live file to ~/work/backups, launchctl kickstart -k gui/501/com.user.dsh-opencode-zen-bridge, heavy-path tool-call turn on :9883 and grep bridge.err.log for tool_call_recovered / stream dropped; core and muse via MR\",\n384|    \"rollback\": \"Restore the backed-up server.py and kickstart the LaunchAgent (< 2 s); revert core and muse via git revert; trigger on any new test failure vs baseline, crash on :9883, non-200 or a raw <tool_invoke> in live content\"\n385|  },\n386|  \"approval\": {\n387|    \"status\": \"NOT_REQUIRED\",\n388|    \"decision_ids\": []\n389|  },\n390|  \"independent_review\": {\n391|    \"required\": true,\n392|    \"status\": \"PASS\",\n393|    \"reviewer\": \"arch-panel-pending\",\n394|    \"evidence_ref\": \"receipts/arch-panel.json\"\n395|  },\n396|  \"open_questions\": [],\n397|  \"protected_paths\": [\n398|    \"analysis/opencode-zen-tool-invoke-fix/handoff-architect.md\",\n399|    \"analysis/opencode-zen-tool-invoke-fix/evidence-ledger.md\"\n400|  ],\n401|  \"materialization\": [],\n402|  \"role_plan\": {\n403|    \"path\": \"plans/architect-01.json\",\n404|    \"sha256\": \"09337bf03bb1ec4979a87fcb926322559e3273e4be3400cc106f1b64bdd5675a\"\n405|  },\n406|  \"deferred\": []\n407|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3ab","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a16f29-8a52-78e0-a3b7-ac73629a118d"},"sequence":48,"recorded_at":1780531400000091,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a16f29-9139-7d63-bf27-9f131bb65f9f","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"01a16f29-9139-7d63-bf27-9f131bb65f9f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"01a16f29-9139-7d63-bf27-9f131bb65f9f"},"call_id":"call_01a16f29cf46761bb6c168efa6addae3","text":"Read text file `/Users/aazhiry1/tmp/cli-agent-bridge/opencode-zen-tool-invoke-fix/.ai-team/runs/opencode-zen-tool-invoke-fix-20261024/coder.json`.\n1|{\n2|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0\",\n3|  \"role\": \"coder\",\n4|  \"task_id\": \"OPENCODE-ZEN-TOOL-INVOKE-FIX\",\n5|  \"iteration\": 1,\n6|  \"status\": \"DONE\",\n7|  \"summary\": \"Re-baselined the untracked opencode-zen-bridge copy on current live (sha 90b1d664…, 3902 lines), wrote red tests first, then implemented AD-001..AD-004 with the ARCH_PANEL Skeptic hardening: trailing-brace recovery (1..16 extra '}', RecursionError-safe, quiet flag against log amplification) and OpenAI 'function' unwrap in opencode-zen/core/muse; _strip_broken_tool_blocks (fail-closed at the 17th candidate) wired into _sanitize_assistant_text, _incomplete_tool_step_prompt, _stream_sse and _serve_json with a one-line notice when nothing else is visible. VER-001/003/004 green, VER-002 failure set identical to the 3-test baseline. Nothing committed or deployed; live ~/.dsh bridge and ~/work/src/cli-agent-bridge untouched.\",\n8|  \"changed_files\": [\n9|    \"bridges/opencode-zen-bridge/server.py\",\n10|    \"bridges/opencode-zen-bridge/tests/test_lenient_tool_call.py\",\n11|    \"bridges/opencode-zen-bridge/tests/test_step_interruption.py\",\n12|    \"core/tool_emulation.py\",\n13|    \"bridges/muse-bridge/server.py\",\n14|    \"tests/test_tool_parser.py\"\n15|  ],\n16|  \"commands\": [\n17|    {\n18|      \"command\": \"python3 -m unittest tests.test_tool_parser -v\",\n19|      \"exit_code\": 0\n20|    },\n21|    {\n22|      \"command\": \"cd bridges/opencode-zen-bridge && python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t . (failure set == baseline: 3 test_unmapped_* tests; Ran 378, errors=0)\",\n23|      \"exit_code\": 1\n24|    },\n25|    {\n26|      \"command\": \"cd bridges/opencode-zen-bridge && python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t . -k negative_control -k unparsed_block_returned_as_text -k closed_batch_without_intermediate_close_kept -k sanitize_closed_alt_batch_kept -k broken_block -k history_renders_tool_calls (Ran 12)\",\n27|      \"exit_code\": 0\n28|    },\n29|    {\n30|      \"command\": \"cd bridges/opencode-zen-bridge && python3 -c <VER-004 verbatim logic> (0.318/0.15/1.992 ms)\",\n31|      \"exit_code\": 0\n32|    },\n33|    {\n34|      \"command\": \"uvx ruff check core/tool_emulation.py bridges/muse-bridge/server.py tests/test_tool_parser.py\",\n35|      \"exit_code\": 0\n36|    },\n37|    {\n38|      \"command\": \"python3 -m unittest discover -s tests (repo root, Ran 899; 2 failures reproduce on clean HEAD: test_b_guard.test_tm018_live_check_subprocess, test_muse_bridge_killpg.test_t00_models_and_health_include_wonder_models_400k)\",\n39|      \"exit_code\": 1\n40|    }\n41|  ],\n42|  \"acceptance_coverage\": [\n43|    {\n44|      \"requirement_id\": \"REQ-001\",\n45|      \"status\": \"COVERED\",\n46|      \"evidence\": \"_loads_lenient/_recover_trailing_braces (+core/muse _loads_tolerant); tests test_trailing_braces_recovered, test_production_payload_single_call, test_trailing_garbage_not_recovered, contract cases trailing_braces*; stream/json single-spawn tests\"\n47|    },\n48|    {\n49|      \"requirement_id\": \"REQ-002\",\n50|      \"status\": \"COVERED\",\n51|      \"evidence\": \"_strip_broken_tool_blocks at _stream_sse sink, _serve_json and _incomplete_tool_step_prompt; test_stream_broken_block_not_in_sse_nor_reprompt, test_json_broken_block_not_in_content_nor_reprompt, test_stream_notice_when_only_broken_block, test_serve_json_*; fail-closed cap test_strip_cap_is_fail_closed and test_strip_scan_is_bounded_broken_block\"\n52|    },\n53|    {\n54|      \"requirement_id\": \"REQ-003\",\n55|      \"status\": \"COVERED\",\n56|      \"evidence\": \"_sanitize_assistant_text strips closed malformed blocks (quiet); test_sanitize_strips_malformed_closed_tool_invoke; kept-batch tests unchanged and green; OpenAI function wrapper parity in all three parsers\"\n57|    },\n58|    {\n59|      \"requirement_id\": \"REQ-004\",\n60|      \"status\": \"COVERED\",\n61|      \"evidence\": \"18 new tests in bridges/opencode-zen-bridge (VER-002 378 = 360 + 18), 8 new in tests/test_tool_parser.py (VER-001 52 = 44 + 8), red phase observed before the fix\"\n62|    }\n63|  ],\n64|  \"assumptions\": [\n65|    \"Live opencode-zen server.py changed again between arch-spec (sha 5f6b7cb0, 3885 lines) and re-baseline (sha 90b1d664, 3902 lines); all anchors were re-resolved by symbol. The rollout sha guard must compare live against 90b1d66499dceadac24f7990423b4c53b2ebd5b23247aaf50efe187851598b9e and merge-file if it moved again.\",\n66|    \"Fail-closed cap (brief/ARCH_PANEL k=1) supersedes the fail-open wording of arch-spec 4.3 step 2: the 17th candidate outside markdown code drops the rest of the text.\",\n67|    \"The three pre-existing baseline failures (test_unmapped_*) are baseline debt: neither fixed nor regressed.\",\n68|    \"The log label for the cap is tool_strip_cap_hit (not tool_block_strip_cap_reached): the 28-char label was masked to '***' by _mask_secrets (24+ char token rule).\"\n69|  ],\n70|  \"risks\": [\n71|    \"The cap counts every candidate outside markdown code, valid ones included: a replayed history message with more than 16 separately closed blocks loses the 17th and later ones in _sanitize_assistant_text (sinks never see valid blocks).\",\n72|    \"Google-direct stream path (_stream_google, own ToolCallParser/emit_content) is not routed through the strip sink; out of scope of arch-spec 4.4 and of the incident (GLM via opencode CLI).\",\n73|    \"opencode-zen _normalize_arguments now also accepts a string-encoded arguments object with extra trailing '}' because it goes through _loads_lenient (core/muse _normalize_arguments stay strict).\",\n74|    \"Root-suite failures test_b_guard.test_tm018_live_check_subprocess and test_muse_bridge_killpg.test_t00_models_and_health_include_wonder_models_400k are environment-dependent and fail identically on clean HEAD.\",\n75|    \"Not deployed: heavy-path check on :9883 and launchctl kickstart (arch-spec 9 rollout steps 2-5) remain for the orchestrator/verifier; bridges/opencode-zen-bridge/ is git-untracked, nothing committed.\"\n76|  ],\n77|  \"open_questions\": [],\n78|  \"next_role\": \"reviewer\",\n79|  \"role_plan\": {\n80|    \"path\": \"plans/coder-01.json\",\n81|    \"sha256\": \"6c47bd81d6c0468e8b03b93199bc919d3d80a3744097cefe2d1c8e3720bfe5bb\"\n82|  }\n83|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
